The Example section of PEP 255 defines a `Tree` class and two versions of an `inorder` generator — one recursive and one non-recursive:

```python
class Tree:
    def __init__(self, label, left=None, right=None):
        self.label = label
        self.left = left
        self.right = right

def inorder(t):
    if t:
        for x in inorder(t.left):
            yield x
        yield t.label
        for x in inorder(t.right):
            yield x
```

